Today a link dropped by the structure pass (ADR-0022) leaves its add event in the history with no matching removal, and the copy that made the link drops it a second time on its next sync because both sides hold the same add event and the no-event fallback brings it back (see the structure() docstring in internal/sync/structure.go). If the merge wrote a removal event for the drop, with an ID derived deterministically from the dropped add event so every copy produces the same event, the making copy would lose the link by the ordinary latest-event rule, the second report would go away, and show --history would show the removal with its reason. Needs: an actor name for merge-authored events, the ID scheme, amendments to ADR-0021 (the merge adds no events) and ADR-0022, and simulator invariants that allow the event.